---
/**
 * Explains demo data handling and the current limits of the inquiry workflow.
 *
 * Dependencies: BaseLayout.
 * Depended on by: Form consent context and the footer.
 * Why this exists: Visitors need plain-language privacy expectations before submitting details.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Justin LeBlanc Booking Demo" canonicalPath="/privacy">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Demo privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Only share what the event needs.</h1>
      <p>
        This page describes the intended isolated demo behavior. Final production retention,
        recording, and contact policies require owner approval before launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <article class="section reading-shell prose">
    <h2>Information the inquiry uses</h2>
    <p>
      The form asks for contact information, event details, requested atmosphere, known timing,
      production and access notes, and consent to follow up. Billing details are not required to
      capture an inquiry. Do not submit payment-card data or sensitive personal records.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it is used</h2>
    <p>
      Submitted details are used to review the event, respond to the inquiry, prepare a consultation,
      and demonstrate the booking workflow. Marketing consent is separate, optional, and unchecked.
    </p>

    <h2>AI chat and voice</h2>
    <p>
      The chat and voice assistants identify themselves as AI. They can explain reviewed booking
      information and help structure an inquiry. They cannot confirm a date or final price. Voice
      recording and transcript behavior must be explicitly configured and disclosed before live use.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
    <p>
      The intended demo retention default is 30 days, subject to final configuration. The event form
      keeps an unsent draft in this browser session so a visitor can move between steps. The server
      stores a submitted record only after it returns a persisted inquiry reference.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Intended funnel events are inquiry submitted, consultation scheduled, hold created, and show
      confirmed. Names, email addresses, phone numbers, event dates, venue notes, free text, and
      invoice contents must not be sent in analytics payloads.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and final policy</h2>
    <p>
      This demo is not the final production privacy policy. Use Justin's
      <a href="https://justinleblancmusic.com/contact" rel="external">current contact page</a> for
      existing-site questions. The owner must approve production recipients, retention, deletion,
      and any recording policy before launch.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
